Hi Glenn,

I've attached the final report for Communicating in Workplace Meetings. Of th=
e 24 people in the group, 22 submitted the final exercise. Of those 22, 17 me=
t all four conditional proposal criteria: an action and its scope, a supporti=
ng fact from the agenda, the staffing coordinator's confirmation by Thursday =
noon, and the action to take if the key rota remains unconfirmed. Five submis=
sions did not yet meet all four criteria; two people did not submit and were =
not assessed.

The report describes the written exercise, rather than course completion or a=
 change in workplace behaviour. The Saturday trial was a practice scenario, s=
o these results do not tell us whether it went ahead.

For a future group, one possible five-minute practice would start with the un=
confirmed condition: ask participants to say first which weekday arrangement =
will remain, then add the confirmation condition and the proposed Saturday tr=
ial. That should give them a chance to make the alternative explicit before p=
utting the whole proposal together.

Thank you for bringing the maintenance agenda to our planning conversation. P=
lease let me know if you'd like to talk through the report.

Best,
Heather

Heather Callahan
Elmwood Adult Learning Cooperative

